---
name: review-task
version: 2.0.0
description: lead phase-ending code review assignment for atm-bd-orchestration. task_id is a review bead the lead creates under the phase feature. Read-only; the lead files the findings as finding beads.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - phase
  - branch
  - commit
  - worktree_path
  - review_focus
  - review_questions
  - references
optional_variables:
  - lead
  - cc
defaults:
  lead: team-lead
  cc: team-lead
metadata:
  type: review-task
  tags:
    - stage:review
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: phase
      variable: phase
    state: review-start
    stage: review
    transition: start
---
<atm-review id="{{ task_id }}" phase="{{ phase }}">
  <description><![CDATA[Phase-ending code review of the top of the phase stack. Read-only analysis only; no code changes.]]></description>

  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>

  <review-focus><![CDATA[
{{ review_focus | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></review-focus>

  <review-questions><![CDATA[
{{ review_questions | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></review-questions>

  <references><![CDATA[
{{ references | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></references>

  <output-format><![CDATA[
    Structured findings report with sections:
    1. SUMMARY — one-paragraph verdict
    2. FINDINGS — numbered list, each with severity (blocking, important, minor), location, finding, recommendation
    3. EXTRACTION-READINESS — score 1-5 per relevant module with rationale
    4. RECOMMENDED-NEXT-SPRINTS — concrete follow-up work items
  ]]></output-format>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Claim the bead, then start the task. `BEADS_ACTOR` must equal your `ATM_IDENTITY` (claims and closes are recorded as that actor); if it is empty, pass `--actor "$ATM_IDENTITY"` to every `bd` write. Check that the review bead is ready: `bd ready -n 0 --json | jq -e --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} 'any(.[]; .id == $b)'`. When it prints `true`, run `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --claim`, then `atm task start {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} "<one line: what you will do first>"`. When it prints `false`, do not claim or start: find the root cause (`bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}`, `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'`, `bd show <blocker>`) and report it with `atm send {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} --stdin`, then wait.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Verify that `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}` is on `{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}` with `HEAD` exactly `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`; reject a mismatched or moving checkout. Read relevant source and doc files at the assigned commit with `git show {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}:<path>`. The phase plan is `bd show <phase feature>` and its children (`bd list --parent <phase feature> --all -n 0`).]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[Do not make any code changes and do not write to beads; {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} files each finding as a finding bead from your report.]]></step>
    <step id="d"><![CDATA[Re-verify every cited file:line at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`, never at a newer branch tip or moving worktree state; stale or missing evidence is a finding, not a guess. Then close the bead and the task together: `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "review complete: <verdict>"` and `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/review-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/review-complete-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`, with the vars built from that template's `required_variables` (`task_id`, `phase` and `commit` unchanged) and written outside the repository. Only this close frees your queue.{% if cc and cc != lead %} Copy a one-line summary to `{{ cc | string | cdata_escape }}` with a plain `atm send {{ cc | string | cdata_escape }} --stdin`.{% endif %}]]></step>
    <step id="d1"><![CDATA[If the review cannot be performed, return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "<reason>"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-review>
